<Base title="Contribute" description="How to support AVI's advocacy work.">
  <h1>Contribute</h1>

  <p>
    AVI's advocacy — litigation, evidence review, and public correction of
    misinformation — is funded by individual contributions, not by industry.
    Contributions are received and accounted for through
    <strong>Harm Reduction Policy &amp; Research Pvt. Ltd. (HRPR)</strong>,
    an MCA-registered company, recorded as company income, audited annually
    and taxed accordingly.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Contributions are not tax-deductible.</strong> HRPR does not
    hold 80G status, so no tax receipt can be issued against your
    contribution.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can contribute</h2>
  <p>
    We can currently accept contributions only from <strong>Indian
    residents, and Indian citizens living abroad remitting from their own
    funds</strong>. Foreign nationals and foreign-registered entities cannot
    contribute directly to this fund — Indian law (FCRA, 2010) restricts
    unregistered organisations from accepting contributions of foreign
    origin, and HRPR does not hold FCRA registration.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you represent an institution abroad interested in supporting
    specific research or policy work, please write to <a href="mailto:contact@vapeindia.org">contact@vapeindia.org</a> — this
    can be structured as commissioned project work, which is handled separately.
  </p>

